# PR repo-guards checklist — run before every `git push`

`repo-guards` blocks `ci-gate-repo`. **Do not push a PR branch until every item below passes locally.**

## 1. DCO Signed-off-by (every commit)

Every non-bot commit in the PR must contain a `Signed-off-by:` line.

```bash
# Preferred: sign at commit time
git commit -s -m "fix(scope): message"

# If amending the latest commit only (branch not shared yet):
git commit --amend -s --no-edit
```

PowerShell has no heredoc — use `git commit -s -m "title" -m "body" -m "Signed-off-by: ..."` or amend with `-s`.

## 2. Tracked issue (before opening the PR)

Create the issue **first** using a repo template (`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`). Section headers must match **exactly** (case and wording):

| Template | Required `##` sections |
| --- | --- |
| Bug report | `Summary`, `Expected behavior`, `Actual behavior`, `Reproduction steps` |
| Feature request | `Problem`, `Proposed solution`, `Acceptance criteria` |

**Not accepted:** `## Expected`, `## Actual`, `## Reproduction` — use full names above.

Bidirectional link (both required before push):

1. PR body: `Closes #NNN` (or Fixes/Resolves)
2. Issue body or comment: `Implementation PR: #NNN`

Issue must be **open** when the PR is opened.

## 3. PR body template (all sections required)

From `.github/pull_request_template.md` — every section header must be present:

- `## What and Why`
- `## How`
- `## Testing`
- `## Performance`
- `## Security`
- `## Migrations / Ops`
- `## Docs`

Store drafts in `ibex-harness-workspace/pr-bodies/` (outside git). Use `gh pr create --body-file`.

## 4. Pre-push verification commands

```bash
# DCO on commits in branch (replace BASE with main merge-base)
git log --format='%B' $(git merge-base main HEAD)..HEAD | grep -qi '^Signed-off-by:' || echo "MISSING DCO"

# Optional when gh is available and PR exists
gh pr view --json body -q .body   # confirm close keyword + sections
gh issue view NNN --json body -q .body   # confirm template sections + PR link
```

## 5. After push

Watch `repo-guards` and `ci-gate-repo` on the PR before declaring success:

```bash
gh pr checks <PR_NUMBER> | grep -E 'repo-guards|ci-gate-repo'
```

If `repo-guards` fails, read the log step name — fix DCO or issue/PR tracking, then re-run (do not stack blind retries).
